jobs
Usage: jobs [-l]

List the jobs started from this shell and their state: Running, Stopped,
or Done.

	-l	also show each job's process id

Jobs are numbered, and %1 refers to job 1.

	sleep 60 &		start one
	jobs			[1] + Running  sleep 60
	fg %1			bring it forward

Jobs belong to one shell. They are not visible from another terminal, and
they die when this shell does -- abduco is what survives that.

See also: fg, bg, kill, ps, abduco
